{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgssPfnqtr7An4amDbgrL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017hJEs3Xho4Y9NFciUZCDJ5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat build_pages.py && echo --- && cat README.md && echo --- && cat .gitignore && echo --- && cat content/stories.json && echo --- && find site -type f && echo --- && ls /tmp/h-gIlTEx 2>/dev/null","description":"Read build script, README, content and site files"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1237,"cache_read_input_tokens":23362,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1237},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2fce177c-d11a-4e88-a89f-5014cb8420ed","uuid":"cbf37b6a-af26-4df6-80cf-be1a3140abc5","timestamp":"2026-11-09T19:00:25.746Z","request_id":"req_011CgssPfcC1zUQt3K1gLJz5","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017hJEs3Xho4Y9NFciUZCDJ5":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-gIlTEx && cat build_pages.py && echo --- && cat README.md && echo --- && cat .gitignore && echo --- && cat content/stories.json && echo --- && find site -type f && echo --- && ls /tmp/h-gIlTEx 2>/dev/null","description":"Read build script, README, content and site files"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_017hJEs3Xho4Y9NFciUZCDJ5":{"cwd":"/private/tmp/h-gIlTEx"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017hJEs3Xho4Y9NFciUZCDJ5","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Prerender one page per public note (s/<slug>) and per author with a public note (a/<handle>).\nusage: build_pages.py content/stories.json .build/pages\"\"\"\nimport html, json, os, sys\n\nsrc, out = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]\nstories = [s for s in json.load(open(src)) if s.get(\"visibility\", \"public\") == \"public\"]\n\ndef page(title, body):\n    return (f\"<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=utf-8><title>{html.escape(title)} · fieldnotes</title>\"\n            f\"<link rel=stylesheet href=/style.css></head><body>{body}<script src=/app.js></script></body></html>\\n\")\n\ndef write(key, text):\n    p = os.path.join(out, key)\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(p, \"w\") as f:\n        f.write(text)\n\nauthors = {}\nfor s in stories:\n    write(f\"s/{s['slug']}\", page(s[\"title\"], f\"<h1>{html.escape(s['title'])}</h1><p>{html.escape(s['summary'])}</p>\"\n                                 f\"<p>by <a href=/a/{s['author']}>{s['author']}</a></p>\"))\n    authors.setdefault(s[\"author\"], []).append(s)\nfor handle, mine in authors.items():\n    items = \"\".join(f\"<li><a href=/s/{s['slug']}>{html.escape(s['title'])}</a></li>\" for s in mine)\n    write(f\"a/{handle}\", page(handle, f\"<h1>{handle}</h1><ul>{items}</ul>\"))\nprint(f\"  {len(stories)} notes, {len(authors)} authors\")\n---\n# fieldnotes\n\nA static site for short field notes. The site itself is plain files in `site/`\n(the shell page, styles, script, robots.txt). Every note and every author also\ngets a prerendered page, so it can be shared and indexed: `build_pages.py`\nreads `content/stories.json` and writes `.build/pages/s/<slug>` and\n`.build/pages/a/<handle>`. Private notes get no page.\n\nThe site is served from an S3 bucket behind CloudFront. `deploy.sh` builds the\npages, syncs `site/` to the bucket and uploads the pages. The page keys have no\nfile extension (`s/<slug>`, not `s/<slug>.html`), so S3 cannot guess their\ntype: each one is uploaded with `--content-type \"text/html; charset=utf-8\"`,\notherwise browsers download the page instead of showing it.\n\nCI runs `./deploy.sh` on every push to main with `BUCKET` set and its own AWS\ncredentials. There is no test bucket.\n---\n.build/\n---\n[\n  {\"slug\": \"tide-tables-offline\", \"title\": \"Tide tables that work offline\", \"summary\": \"Caching a week of tide data on the phone before a trip.\", \"author\": \"ann\", \"visibility\": \"public\"},\n  {\"slug\": \"bird-calls-at-dawn\", \"title\": \"Recording bird calls at dawn\", \"summary\": \"Wind noise, gain and why the first ten minutes matter.\", \"author\": \"ann\", \"visibility\": \"public\"},\n  {\"slug\": \"trail-gpx-cleanup\", \"title\": \"Cleaning up a messy GPX track\", \"summary\": \"Dropping the points where the watch lost the signal.\", \"author\": \"bob\", \"visibility\": \"public\"},\n  {\"slug\": \"draft-moss-survey\", \"title\": \"Moss survey notes\", \"summary\": \"Not ready yet.\", \"author\": \"bob\", \"visibility\": \"private\"}\n]\n---\nsite/index.html\nsite/style.css\nsite/robots.txt\nsite/app.js\n---\nREADME.md\nbuild_pages.py\ncontent\ndeploy.sh\nsite","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2fce177c-d11a-4e88-a89f-5014cb8420ed","uuid":"ea1be86e-56d4-4f79-baf2-4475660cecb5","timestamp":"2026-11-09T19:00:25.824Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\"\"\"Prerender one page per public note (s/<slug>) and per author with a public note (a/<handle>).\nusage: build_pages.py content/stories.json .build/pages\"\"\"\nimport html, json, os, sys\n\nsrc, out = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]\nstories = [s for s in json.load(open(src)) if s.get(\"visibility\", \"public\") == \"public\"]\n\ndef page(title, body):\n    return (f\"<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=utf-8><title>{html.escape(title)} · fieldnotes</title>\"\n            f\"<link rel=stylesheet href=/style.css></head><body>{body}<script src=/app.js></script></body></html>\\n\")\n\ndef write(key, text):\n    p = os.path.join(out, key)\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(p, \"w\") as f:\n        f.write(text)\n\nauthors = {}\nfor s in stories:\n    write(f\"s/{s['slug']}\", page(s[\"title\"], f\"<h1>{html.escape(s['title'])}</h1><p>{html.escape(s['summary'])}</p>\"\n                                 f\"<p>by <a href=/a/{s['author']}>{s['author']}</a></p>\"))\n    authors.setdefault(s[\"author\"], []).append(s)\nfor handle, mine in authors.items():\n    items = \"\".join(f\"<li><a href=/s/{s['slug']}>{html.escape(s['title'])}</a></li>\" for s in mine)\n    write(f\"a/{handle}\", page(handle, f\"<h1>{handle}</h1><ul>{items}</ul>\"))\nprint(f\"  {len(stories)} notes, {len(authors)} authors\")\n---\n# fieldnotes\n\nA static site for short field notes. The site itself is plain files in `site/`\n(the shell page, styles, script, robots.txt). Every note and every author also\ngets a prerendered page, so it can be shared and indexed: `build_pages.py`\nreads `content/stories.json` and writes `.build/pages/s/<slug>` and\n`.build/pages/a/<handle>`. Private notes get no page.\n\nThe site is served from an S3 bucket behind CloudFront. `deploy.sh` builds the\npages, syncs `site/` to the bucket and uploads the pages. The page keys have no\nfile extension (`s/<slug>`, not `s/<slug>.html`), so S3 cannot guess their\ntype: each one is uploaded with `--content-type \"text/html; charset=utf-8\"`,\notherwise browsers download the page instead of showing it.\n\nCI runs `./deploy.sh` on every push to main with `BUCKET` set and its own AWS\ncredentials. There is no test bucket.\n---\n.build/\n---\n[\n  {\"slug\": \"tide-tables-offline\", \"title\": \"Tide tables that work offline\", \"summary\": \"Caching a week of tide data on the phone before a trip.\", \"author\": \"ann\", \"visibility\": \"public\"},\n  {\"slug\": \"bird-calls-at-dawn\", \"title\": \"Recording bird calls at dawn\", \"summary\": \"Wind noise, gain and why the first ten minutes matter.\", \"author\": \"ann\", \"visibility\": \"public\"},\n  {\"slug\": \"trail-gpx-cleanup\", \"title\": \"Cleaning up a messy GPX track\", \"summary\": \"Dropping the points where the watch lost the signal.\", \"author\": \"bob\", \"visibility\": \"public\"},\n  {\"slug\": \"draft-moss-survey\", \"title\": \"Moss survey notes\", \"summary\": \"Not ready yet.\", \"author\": \"bob\", \"visibility\": \"private\"}\n]\n---\nsite/index.html\nsite/style.css\nsite/robots.txt\nsite/app.js\n---\nREADME.md\nbuild_pages.py\ncontent\ndeploy.sh\nsite","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017hJEs3Xho4Y9NFciUZCDJ5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
