{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgssWXk7CPFHqjQE51iVf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`deploy.sh` now removes bucket keys that the build no longer produces, so deleted or private notes and files removed from `site/` disappear on the next deploy. I wrote up the details in `ANSWER.md`. I didn't deploy or touch a real bucket.\n\n**What changed**\n- The `site/` sync no longer uses `--delete`. It would otherwise remove the page keys, which live in the same bucket.\n- Pages are still uploaded in place, so a live page is overwritten rather than deleted and never 404s during the deploy.\n- A new `prune_stale` step runs after the uploads. It lists the bucket and deletes any key that is neither a `site/` file nor a built page. It refuses to run if the build produced nothing, so a broken build can't empty the bucket.\n\n**Verification**\n- I ran the script against a mock `aws` backed by a local directory. The stale and private pages and the removed `site/` file were deleted. Live pages were overwritten, never deleted. All uploads ran before any delete.\n- When the bucket listing failed, the script exited non-zero and deleted nothing.\n- The mock tests the script's logic, not the real CLI. A dry run against a test bucket would confirm the `aws` calls behave as I expect, including how an empty bucket lists.\n\n**Colleague's note:** I applied the core idea (a `--delete` must not cover keys another step uploads) and the in-place overwrite and post-upload prune. I did not use the `--exclude` filters, because I couldn't test their deletion semantics here. The worklore-specific prefixes and the polling check need a live deploy, so they don't apply as written. `ANSWER.md` lists each part.\n\nThe changes are uncommitted on `main`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2027,"cache_read_input_tokens":45333,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2027},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2fce177c-d11a-4e88-a89f-5014cb8420ed","uuid":"54d8c91e-d845-4658-bbdf-1cb6df8788c2","timestamp":"2026-11-09T19:02:01.108Z","request_id":"req_011CgssWXaSRcED3vQjyzw3x"}
